{"answer": "{
  "findings": [
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:710",
      "fact": "Class Research2Runner is the reusable core. It owns console, programmer, plan_module, results_module, run_id, board_root, stage_dir, current_stage, current_case, boot, boots, selection, completed_cases, flashed_roles."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1007",
      "fact": "_run_one_case(stage, role, case) is the per-case execution unit. It validates case id and argv, creates host run_dir, writes board-command.txt, captures before state, records argv.txt, runs the framed CLI, captures after state, calls _collect_and_transfer, writes metadata.json, enforces exit==0/taint==0/framed-exit agreement, validates record.json, writes metrics.json and SAVED."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1055",
      "fact": "_run_one_case calls self._collect_and_transfer(cid, board_case_dir, run_dir) dynamically, so a thin subclass can override the archive routine and still reuse the existing capture/metadata/validation flow."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1024",
      "fact": "The board case command is exactly: cd board_case_dir && board_cli argv > record.json 2> stderr.txt; ec=$?; echo \"$ec\" > exit.txt, wrapped by SerialConsole.run_shell(cwd=...)."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1112",
      "fact": "_run_one_case gates on exit_code present and ==0, framed_exit==exit.txt, and taint_after strip()=='0'. These are the tested zero-exit/taint semantics."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1140",
      "fact": "_verify_stage_saved(stage, cases) requires every case dir to contain record.json, record.sha256, metadata.json, archive.tar.gz, archive.sha256, archive.b64, SAVED; re-hashes archive and record; requires metadata exit==0 and taint_after=='0'."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1167",
      "fact": "_run_stage(stage, role) calls _sync before a subsequent flash when flashed_roles is non-empty, calls _flash once for that stage, waits for root, collects boot info, checks boot change, calls build_plan(stage), writes plan.json and plan.sha256.json, optionally freezes selection, resolves and runs each case through _run_one_case, then calls _verify_stage_saved and writes stage-done.json."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1209",
      "fact": "Existing _run_stage automatically calls _freeze_selection(stage, cases) at the first case needing selection. This is the behavior the new method88 runner must not use when plan+selection are supplied/frozen externally."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1224",
      "fact": "Existing run() hardcodes stages: e2=>role1 and method=>role2, then loops _run_stage. It does not support two stages both role2 or supplied plan/selection."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1242",
      "fact": "run() only appends ('e2',1) and ('method',2). New method88 two-boot same-role flow needs a new stage orchestration layer or an overridden run()."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1253",
      "fact": "COMPLETE.json stores boots keyed by role. For two role2 boots, the second boot overwrites the first in that summary, although each stage writes its own boot.json at scripts/mac_research2.py:1182."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:849",
      "fact": "_check_boot_change(role, boot) compares against previously recorded boot_ids. Same-role reuse works for comparison only if the previous role2 entry is retained until the second boot is checked; current self.boots[role]=boot then overwrites the first role2 entry."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:806",
      "fact": "_collect_boot_info(role) performs post-flash board queries: uname -r, sha256sum board_cli, --caps2, and cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id. boot_id is read raw from the board file and checked non-empty."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:528",
      "fact": "OpenFPGALoaderProgrammer.flash(bit_path) runs exactly one openFPGALoader subprocess per call and raises TechnicalFailure on timeout or nonzero rc. There is no retry."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1176",
      "fact": "Each _run_stage performs exactly one _flash(image) call. Two method88 boots mean exactly two _flash calls, one per stage."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1172",
      "fact": "The only pre-next-flash sync is in _run_stage: if flashed_roles is non-empty, _sync() must exit 0 before the next BIT flash. For method88 this is the safe barrier between boot1 and boot2."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:774",
      "fact": "_sync() runs board command 'sync' and raises TechnicalFailure on nonzero exit."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:784",
      "fact": "_wait_for_root(timeout) uses framed harmless 'true' probes and does not re-run experiments. It is the default readiness barrier after flash."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/run_research2_mac.py:15",
      "fact": "Adapter LoggedInRunner drains console input before _flash, then calls super()._flash. This is the tested read-before-flash behavior for avoiding stale UART/boot output in the frame buffer."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/run_research2_mac.py:20",
      "fact": "Adapter _wait_for_root waits for fresh boot evidence ('Linux version ' or 'login:'), then a root prompt, handles login/Password prompts, sends 'root\\r', limits attempts to 6, and finally delegates to super()._wait_for_root(remaining)."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:948",
      "fact": "Original _collect_and_transfer archives with 'tar -czf <archive_path> -C <board_case_dir> .'. This is the command that failed under BusyBox tar with exit=1."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/continue_research2_transfer.py:12",
      "fact": "Recovery adapter PackingConsole intercepts commands starting with 'tar -czf ', parses them, and replaces them with a BusyBox-compatible tar -cf plus gzip -c recipe."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/continue_research2_transfer.py:18",
      "fact": "Tested workaround command shape: test ! -e <plain> && test ! -e <target> && tar -cf <plain> -C <source> . && gzip -c <plain> > <target>. It rejects overwrite of either the target .tar.gz or the intermediate .plain.tar."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/continue_research2_transfer.py:41",
      "fact": "Recovery script checks the old metadata transfer_error for 'tar exit=1' before attempting recovery, confirming the observed failure mode was the archive step."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/continue_research2_transfer.py:59",
      "fact": "Recovery script demonstrates the reusable interfaces: it starts SerialConsole, checks existing shell, calls _collect_boot_info(1), compares boot_id to old run, checks frozen plan equality, calls _collect_and_transfer without re-running CLI, validates retained record, writes metadata/metrics/SAVED, then calls _run_one_case for remaining cases, _verify_stage_saved, and _run_stage('method',2)."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/mac-research-two-bit-20261003/host-tools/continue_research2_transfer.py:90",
      "fact": "Recovery script calls runner._run_one_case('e2', 1, runner._resolve_case(case, None)) for missing e2 cases and runner._verify_stage_saved('e2', plan['cases']) before _run_stage('method',2). This confirms _run_one_case and _verify_stage_saved are viable subclass reuse points."
    },
    {
      "citation": "tests/test_mac_research2.py:592",
      "fact": "Existing plan test asserts build_plan('method') count is 462 and includes calibration/reference/formal/boundary/holdout counts. That is not the new 88-case plan."
    },
    {
      "citation": "tests/test_mac_research2.py:608",
      "fact": "Existing tests assert resolve_case is strictly two-argument and that selection is applied through resolve_case. A supplied frozen selection must still be passed through resolve_case for cases that need it."
    },
    {
      "citation": "tests/test_mac_research2.py:691",
      "fact": "Existing end-to-end tests cover the old e2 role1 then method role2 sequence, archive-on-technical-failure, first-stage hash break blocking second flash, and unchanged boot_id stopping after second flash. They do not cover two role2 boots, role2-only packages, supplied plan/selection, or BusyBox tar workaround."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:236",
      "fact": "load_manifest currently requires images to be a list of exactly two entries, and roles must be exactly {1,2}. A role2-only manifest cannot validate under the existing research2-delivery-v1 loader."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:267",
      "fact": "verify_manifest_package_files verifies every image entry. If an old two-image manifest is reused for role2-only operation, the unused role1 BIT must still be present and hash-verify."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:264",
      "fact": "verify_manifest_package_files does not verify any top-level plans section. The existing DELIVERY.json plans section is therefore not checked by current preflight."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/research-two-bit-20261003/delivery/DELIVERY.json:18",
      "fact": "Old delivery manifest contains a plans section for e2 and method with path/count/sha256, but mac_research2.py load_manifest ignores it. New method88 plan/selection hashes need explicit verification in the new runner/preflight or a manifest schema extension."
    },
    {
      "citation": "out/research-two-bit-20261003/delivery/DELIVERY.json:213",
      "fact": "scripts.plan points to scripts/research2_plan.py (code), not to the JSON plan. Existing preflight verifies code hashes, not frozen plan JSON."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:289",
      "fact": "run_preflight is board-side-effect-free with respect to CLI/cases: it loads manifest, verifies package files, checks openFPGALoader and pyserial, briefly opens and closes the serial port, and prints JSON. It does not run --caps2 or any board experiment case."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:301",
      "fact": "Preflight serial openness is checked by opening Serial(serial_port, ...) and immediately closing. This matches the allowed existing preflight style."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1290",
      "fact": "main calls run_preflight before requiring --out or checking out-dir existence, so preflight does not create an output directory."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:1225",
      "fact": "run() creates out_dir with exist_ok=False, and main rejects an existing --out. This enforces no overwrite and no resume for a normal run."
    },
    {
      "citation": "scripts/mac_research2.py:626",
      "fact": "safe_extract_tar_gz rejects absolute paths, traversal, backslashes/NUL, duplicates, links, devices/fifos, nested entries, and entries outside the allowlist. CASE_ARCHIVE_FILES is defined at scripts/mac_research2.py:68."
    },
    {
      "citation": "tests/test_mac_research2.py:397",
      "fact": "Existing safe-extract tests cover traversal, symlink, duplicate entry, entries outside the allowlist, and acceptance of './record.json' style entries."
    },
    {
      "citation": "docs/mac-research2.md:230",
      "fact": "Documented known limitation states JTAG flash resets FPGA and Linux state is not maintained. This supports the new runner rule: no hot Linux reconfigure; loading BIT restarts the system as the existing flow."
    }
  ],
